# Copy to .env.local and fill in. Every value here is PUBLIC - it is compiled
# into the bundle a browser downloads, so nothing secret belongs in this file
# or in any VITE_ variable. The signing keys are server-held and the frontend
# holds no credentials at all.
#
# The URLs below are not placeholders. csp.parity.test.ts reads this file and
# asserts that every origin the deployed Content-Security-Policy permits is one
# some VITE_*_URL here actually points at, and vice versa. An empty value makes
# that comparison fall back to a pinned list, which is a check that no longer
# compares anything - so a real deployment's origin belongs here.

# The Supabase project the deployed app talks to. Must match the origin in
# vercel.json's connect-src, both https: and wss:.
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://hvuzifnonhrqaqwglwbz.supabase.co

# The publishable (anon) key. Public by design: it identifies the project and
# carries no privileges beyond what row-level security grants an anonymous or
# signed-in caller. NEVER put a service-role key in any VITE_ variable - it
# would ship to every browser.
VITE_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=

# Where the published chain head is read from, with {society} substituted.
# Deliberately EMPTY: no anchor is published yet, and the parity suite asserts
# that emptiness as a pair, so setting this without adding its origin to
# vercel.json's connect-src fails a test rather than silently blocking the
# fetch in production - where a blocked anchor read is indistinguishable from a
# society whose head has never been published.
VITE_ANCHOR_URL=

# Offers the local seed accounts on the sign-in screen. Dev server only; a
# production build never carries them.
VITE_DEMO_LOGINS=
